cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use the SSIT in your research, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "Stochastic System Identification Toolkit (SSIT)"
abstract: >-
  MATLAB toolkit to specify and solve the Chemical Master Equation (CME) for
  discrete stochastic models of single-cell gene regulation. The SSIT supports
  finite state projection (FSP), stochastic simulation (SSA), moment and ODE
  analyses, sensitivity analysis, Fisher information and experiment design,
  and parameter inference (MLE, Metropolis-Hastings, ABC) from single-cell
  data such as smFISH.
